Mixed-license repository
========================

This repository contains both project-authored material and reconstructed
historical program content. A single repository-wide open-source license does
not apply to every file.

1. Project-authored material
----------------------------

Except where a file or section states otherwise, original material created for
this recovery project is licensed under the MIT License in LICENSE-MIT. This
includes the project's build and verification scripts, original recovery
documentation, analysis, annotations, and project-created data to the extent
those materials are copyrightable and do not reproduce third-party content.

2. Historical IBM/Microsoft program content
--------------------------------------------

The reconstructed IBM Cassette BASIC C1.10 program content, including the
instruction stream, tables, strings, constants, and any byte-exact ROM image
produced from it, is NOT licensed under the MIT License by this project.

In particular, src/basic110_C1.10_recovered_phase16_exact.asm is excluded from
the repository-wide MIT grant as a complete work because it reconstructs
historical IBM/Microsoft program content. Project-authored comments, semantic
labels, and annotations within that file are MIT-licensed only to the extent
they are separately copyrightable and separable from the historical program
content.

No license statement in this repository grants rights in IBM, Microsoft, or
other third-party copyrights, trademarks, or other intellectual property.

3. ROM images
-------------

Reference ROM images are not tracked in the Git repository. Build output with
.rom or .bin extensions is ignored. If a user supplies a reference ROM for
verification, that file remains outside the project's license grant.

See COPYRIGHT_AND_LICENSE.md for the repository's copyright and provenance
statement and LICENSE-MIT for the MIT terms that apply to project-authored
material.
